From: A2Tools-patch <patch@localhost>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 23:04:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 29/30] Plugins: an order the player sets, for the dock's tabs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Settings → Plugins → Installed has arrows to move a plugin up or down;
the plugin dock's tabs follow that order. The meter keeps it
(`dpsMeter.pluginOrder`), so it survives a restart and the dock's own
storage.

The dock's tabs were meant to be dragged into order, but on Linux the
window's file drop handler took the drag and nothing moved. The dock
window no longer has one, and a tab dragged there sets the same order.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RahWACwaxzLAcYgwc9jk8C
